  "chapter": {
    "number": 131,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(132) A Song of Degrees."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Lord, remember David, and all his meekness:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "how he swore to the Lord, and vowed to the God of Jacob, saying,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "noteId": 237
          },
          {
            "text": "I will not go into the tabernacle of my house; I will not go up to the couch of my bed;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will not give sleep to my eyes, nor slumber to my eyelids, nor rest to my temples,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "until I find a place for the Lord, a tabernacle for the God of Jacob.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Behold, we heard of it in Ephratha; we found it in the fields of the wood.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let us enter into his tabernacles: let us worship at the place where his feet stood.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Arise, O Lord, into your rest; you, and the ark of your holiness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Your priests shall clothe themselves with righteousness; and your saints shall exult.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the sake of your servant David turn not away the face of your anointed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord swore in truth to David, and he will not annul it, saying, Of the fruit of your body will I set a king upon your throne.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "If your children will keep my covenant, and these my testimonies which I shall teach them, their children also shall sit upon your throne for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the Lord has elected Sion, he has chosen her for a habitation for himself, saying,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "This is my rest for ever: here will I dwell; for I have chosen it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will surely bless her provision: I will satisfy her poor with bread.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will clothe her priests with salvation; and her saints shall greatly exult.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "There will I cause to spring up a horn to David: I have prepared a lamp for my anointed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "His enemies will I clothe with a shame; but upon himself shall my",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 238
          },
          {
            "text": "holiness flourish.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 237,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. if I shall, etc. Hebraism.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 131,
          "verse": 3
        }
      },
      {
